## Cleanup (mandatory in React)

Always clean up — stale ScrollTriggers cause memory leaks and broken behavior on
hot reload in Next.js.

```tsx
// Option A: kill all in component
useEffect(() => {
  // ... setup ...
  return () => {
    ScrollTrigger.getAll().forEach((t) => t.kill())
  }
}, [])

// Option B: use @gsap/react hook (cleaner)
import { useGSAP } from '@gsap/react'

useGSAP(() => {
  // all ScrollTriggers created here auto-clean on unmount
  ScrollTrigger.create({ ... })
}, { scope: containerRef })
```

---

## `ScrollTrigger.refresh()`

Call after DOM changes that affect scroll height:
- After images load
- After accordion expand/collapse
- After font swap

```ts
ScrollTrigger.refresh()
```

Never call `refresh()` inside `useEffect` with frequent dependencies — it's expensive.
Use it once after async content resolves.

